{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/535855-stealing-charms-using-solar-charms-for-other-splats","id":535855,"title":"Stealing Charms - Using Solar Charms for other Splats","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Solar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-06-01T13:01:52-07:00","id":535855,"title":"Stealing Charms - Using Solar Charms for other Splats","content":"In one of my games, my Storyteller had his Sidereal NPC use Letter within Letter technique (or a custom Sidereal version of it). I though having a charm that allows Sidereals to secretly send messages fits pretty well for the Splat.<br /> <br /> Since everyone and their mother seems to have access to Ox Body and Lunars have access to Keen Sense Technique, so there is precedent for other splats having access to some Solar Charms.<br /> <br /> Here are some ideas I had:<br /> <br /> Sidereals - Harmonious Academic Methology (Lore), Legendary Scholar Curriculum (Lore), Letter within a Letter Technique (Linguistics)<br /> Lunars - Chaos Repelling Pattern (Lore), Wyld-Shaping Technique (Lore), Wyld Cauldron Technology (Lore)<br /> <br /> I also considered running a DB Dynast game with building the Dragonblooded characters with Solar Charms (replace sun imagery with appropriate Elemental Imagery). <br /> <br /> Has anyone else does anything like this in their own games? How did it work out?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":3950,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","user":"wonderandawe","date":". 06-01-2015, 04:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-01T13:19:34-07:00","id":535888,"title":"","content":"Everybody has a Charm <i>called</i> Ox-Body. What they don't have is the <i>same</i> Charm.<br /> <br /> You have to be super, super careful when exporting Solar Charms onto other Exalt types, because Solar Charms are usually a lot more badass, especially at the high end, than the Charms other Exalt types get, and also are often not really entirely appropriate for those Exalt types themes.<br /> <br /> Like, I would never export the 1e or 2e Solar charmtree into the Dragon-Blooded, even if they are probably the Exalt type best suited to receive it. Giving the Dragon-Blooded access to easy perfects of all sorts, easy flurries, the true jaw-dropping insanity of the Solar Athletics and Survival trees? Wyld-Shaping Technique and Wyld Cauldron Technology in the hands of the Realm and Lookshy? I mean, wow. That would be one hell of a gonzo game, for the very brief amount of time it would take for your the Realm and it's thousands upon thousands of Solar charm-users to just completely roll over everyone and everything in their way.<br /> <br /> There's nothing wrong with looking at the occasional Solar Charm and going &quot;yoink!&quot;. I would advise heavily against exporting any charmtree wholesale. Your game has a decent chance of just breaking.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-01T14:07:41-07:00","id":535915,"title":"","content":"I've always toyed with the idea of creating 'ability styles' that aren't martial arts based. The idea there is if you want to make certain charms available to everyone, take part of the tree and make it into a style, maybe add a few extra prereqs, and have it be equivalent to CMA in who can learn it.<br /> <br /> Beyond that, if you only want to take one or two charms, that's likely much safer and easier to do, just make sure those specific charms suit the Exalt type you're giving them to.<br /> <br /> I fully agree with Murcushio though, in that letting Dragonbloods have access to all Solar charms (or even a handful) is a very bad idea and gives you an entirely different setting just by definition of what dragonblood can normally do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-01T14:14:59-07:00","id":535919,"title":"","content":"I didn't consider the implications of thousands of Solar on a Creation-wide level. I was more thinking about backstabbing Dynast politics and the like.<br /> <br /> Let's drop the DB idea and focus on what would make good Solar charms to steal for other splats. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-01T14:41:21-07:00","id":535951,"title":"","content":"I don't think any non-Solar should get Wyld-Shaping Technique or Wyld Cauldron Technology, except for Infernals getting equivalents.<br /> <br /> Also, Infernals don't have Ox-Body Technique, and I don't know about Alchemicals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 06-01-2015, 05:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-01T14:45:00-07:00","id":535952,"title":"","content":"I had this homebrew idea of taking Wyld Shaping away from Solars and giving it to Lunars. It would increase the interconnectiveness between the Solars and Lunars. Lunars go out into the Wyld and get the materials and Solars take the materials and make it into awesome things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-01T14:51:09-07:00","id":535969,"title":"","content":"Well, I feel like it is all about how well the Charm fits with the splat. And whether it is necessary.<br /> <br /> Particularly, if they're already things you can do by stunting Sidereal or Lunar Charms, with an attitude of ST generosity towards stunts and using the Storyteller system, I'd honestly be tempted just to let them do that. Like if your Sidereal wants to teach some NPC and they're have some Charm that makes them amazingly persuasive or able to communicate (Blue Vervain Binding?), I'd just say they can stunt that and the NPC is really inspired and goes off and trains and is now amazingly better at that ability. It's not like it's game breaking or anything and it fits as a capability the Sidereals should have as characters.<br /> <br /> If they want to cook up an whole army, then it should be within Sidereal Astrological capability and general craftiness to weave destiny such that a force of great warriors arises among the people and comes together. What kind of version of Sidereals is acceptable where they *can't* secretly shape fate such that the Outlaws of the Marsh learn their skills and come together, and eventually become the champions of the people? If the Sidereal Astrology and Charm system as it exists can handle this capability, just let the players roll play and stunt their way to it. If it can't, then I don't think adapting the Solar Charm plus asking the player to stunt it with Sidereal flavour is a big deal. But seriously think through whether the players can do it without adapting any Solar Charms first.<br /> <br /> Looking at the other example, Letter Within Letter Technique, does it make sense that the Sidereals *shouldn't* be able to conceal a message cleverly within another message such that only a particular listener can understand it? Given everything we know about the sort of characters Sidereals are meant to be (subtle encoding of messages and recognition of messages not exactly being a weak point of theirs). If so, why not let them have the Charm, or even let them do it without the Charm, just as a stunt (albeit without some of the special qualities granted by the Charm)?<br /> <br /> Or with Lunars and Wyld Shaping Technique, what is it that they need the Charm to do? If it's something which makes sense for them they can achieve it by some other means, they don't really need the Charm. Like, if it makes sense for them to retreive treasure from the Wyld by exploring the Wyld and claiming it from there, just let them do that. If it's making new land, do they really *need* to make new land (Creation has plenty)? And so on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-01T14:56:02-07:00","id":535971,"title":"","content":"Sidereals should have cool training charms, but I think their approach to training should differ from the Solar approach.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-01T14:57:25-07:00","id":535975,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/535855-stealing-charms-using-solar-charms-for-other-splats?p=535952#post535952\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I had this homebrew idea of taking Wyld Shaping away from Solars and giving it to Lunars. It would increase the interconnectiveness between the Solars and Lunars. Lunars go out into the Wyld and get the materials and Solars take the materials and make it into awesome things.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that could work, it would mean Lunars of the second age still have that crazy ability to pull shards of True Ice from the southern wyld, but their ability to forge it into a daiklave is getting close to the limit of what they can do in a reasonable timespan. Pulling all that stuff together into a functional airship would be possible, but without Solar artiface would take forever.<br /> <br /> On the other hand taking it AWAY from Solars, not just giving it to Lunars, sits less well with me. Solars are supposed to be the ultimate masters of sorcery and stuff like that, and going out into the Wyld to summon forth a river of quicksilver in order to make his silver golem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-01T15:09:30-07:00","id":535984,"title":"","content":"Yeah Lunars definitely shouldn't get Solar-level charms to actually craft stuff into things/people/land/creatures.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-01T15:13:47-07:00","id":535986,"title":"","content":"Heh, I'm not sure how much even Solars should get what is historically Solar level Charms to craft stuff into things/people/land/creatures! (And we shall see with 3e...)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-01T15:44:56-07:00","id":536022,"title":"","content":"Lunars already steal Solar charms (then have higher mote costs and a weaker effect). That's about a third of the Lunar charmset.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-01T17:04:40-07:00","id":536191,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/535855-stealing-charms-using-solar-charms-for-other-splats?p=536022#post536022\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lunars already steal Solar charms (then have higher mote costs and a weaker effect). That's about a third of the Lunar charmset.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good example of how not to do it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-01T17:30:35-07:00","id":536271,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/535855-stealing-charms-using-solar-charms-for-other-splats?p=535951#post535951\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think any non-Solar should get Wyld-Shaping Technique or Wyld Cauldron Technology, except for Infernals getting equivalents.<br /> <br /> Also, Infernals don't have Ox-Body Technique, and I don't know about Alchemicals.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hardened Devil Body, Malfeas charm with no prereqs.<br /> <br /> Strain-Resistant Chassis Modification: Stamina 2, no prereqs<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Regarding Solar Charms: I can't comment generally, but the devs have said that they were specifically denying Infernals the ability to do so. Infernal charm clouds mean you have to do things like become unable to sleep without nightmares (in exchange for not needing to sleep at all) before you can continue increasing your damage resistance. This might refer more to the tree structure than the charms themselves.<br /> <br /> I think a better way would be to do it like Alchemicals do, similar but distinct. A sole Alchemical crafter is capped at Essence times faster, but when you get a group of them they can supercharge each other. You end up with CNNT, but it reinforces the themes of the Champions to accomplish their greatest feats while part of something greater.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-01T18:36:05-07:00","id":536330,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exthalion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/535855-stealing-charms-using-solar-charms-for-other-splats?p=536271#post536271\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Regarding Solar Charms: I can't comment generally, but the devs have said that they were specifically denying Infernals the ability to do so.</div> </div> </div> </div>To do what?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-01T20:06:01-07:00","id":536420,"title":"","content":"I'll fully admit that I'm more of a fluff player than a crunch player. I'm not going to be writing my own home brew charms, so I'd figured that I'd try to steal chains from somewhere else (Solar charm set). <br /> <br /> What I am reading here is that this is a bad idea barring a few exceptions. What are they few exceptions? <br /> <br /> Or is this just a bad idea in general and I should just wait until 3rd edition Lunars and Sidereals come out?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-01T21:36:18-07:00","id":536479,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/535855-stealing-charms-using-solar-charms-for-other-splats?p=536330#post536330\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To do what?</div> </div> </div> </div>Learn Solar charms.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/535855-stealing-charms-using-solar-charms-for-other-splats?p=536420#post536420\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll fully admit that I'm more of a fluff player than a crunch player. I'm not going to be writing my own home brew charms, so I'd figured that I'd try to steal chains from somewhere else (Solar charm set).<br /> <br /> What I am reading here is that this is a bad idea barring a few exceptions. What are they few exceptions?<br /> <br /> Or is this just a bad idea in general and I should just wait until 3rd edition Lunars and Sidereals come out?</div> </div> </div> </div>The ones marked with the Eclipse keyword? [/3e joke]<br /> <br /> I think spirit charms are generally safest to steal from. For solar charms, I would guess throw out all the perfects, craft boosters, wyld shaping, and society scale social magic. The Socialize charm that adds 1 to your appearance and prevents you from unintentionally making a fool of yourself is probably safe. The make the Blessed Isle devout Sol worshipers is probably too much.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-02T23:32:30-07:00","id":537813,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/535855-stealing-charms-using-solar-charms-for-other-splats?p=535951#post535951\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think any non-Solar should get Wyld-Shaping Technique or Wyld Cauldron Technology, except for Infernals getting equivalents.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like Abyssals having a Labyrinth-based equivalent, with all the caveats that entails. Otherwise, yes.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/471-cenobite451","name":"Cenobite451","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar471_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"275"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}